Android Vulkan overrides

These files are development inputs for an Android arm64 build of the speech
engine's Vulkan backend. No recipe in this repository compiles them: the
CMakeLists.txt one directory up builds against an engine checkout it is given
as ENGINE_SOURCE and takes ggml from that checkout. A build that uses the
overrides puts them in the place of that checkout's Vulkan backend itself.

Each file in this directory is listed here with where it comes from.

ggml-vulkan.cpp
  A modified copy of ggml's Vulkan backend, src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp,
  which the speech engine carries under external/ggml. ggml is distributed
  under the MIT License reproduced at the end of this notice; the modified
  copy stays under that licence. This repository's Apache-2.0 licence covers
  the three other files in this directory and does not replace ggml's terms
  for this one.

  Upstream revision: 3174e6b26f11a0e39b4f150961dce98f43ba860d of the speech
  engine (audio.cpp), which carries ggml's file at
  external/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp. ggml's own revision inside
  that engine is not recorded. The base was established by comparison: the
  copy here, without its three-line head comment, differs from that file
  (sha256 bf3ca8dcb06f29e866a430e1d546fd6db200c0291a214508e3d7e459cf1daedf
  with line ends as here) in thirteen places, 55 lines added and 20 removed,
  and in nothing else. The file did not enter this repository with that
  record; it was made afterwards, against an engine source whose pinned
  files match the revision.

  The thirteen places, all of them:
    - includes scalar_tile_warp.h and aii_matmul_f32_spv.h (the second is
      generated from aii_matmul_f32.comp by the build that uses the override);
    - the device structure gains the member pipeline_aii_matmul_f32;
    - the scalar matrix-multiply tile configurations (l_warptile, m_warptile,
      s_warptile) take their warp from aii_scalar_tile_warp() where upstream
      took it from the hardware subgroup size;
    - when the environment variable AII_VK_F32_TILED is set, the pipeline
      aii_matmul_f32_tiled is created from aii_matmul_f32_spv;
    - where that pipeline exists, a multiplication of two F32 matrices that
      needs no dequantisation uses it; such a multiplication with contiguous
      operands is kept off the matrix-vector path; and it is not fused with a
      following operation, so that the add node is computed and not dropped;
    - before a result is read back through a host-coherent mapping, a memory
      barrier from the writing stage to the host's read is recorded: the
      fence alone says the work ended, not that the host may read it;
    - the submission that waits for a graph's completion is a real command
      that carries that dependency with the fence, in place of a submission
      with no command (five of the thirteen places), because on a physical
      phone the empty submission returned while mapped output still changed.

scalar_tile_warp.h
  Written for this project. Apache-2.0, as the repository.

aii_matmul_f32.comp
  Written for this project: a compute shader for F32 matrix multiplication.
  Its push-constant block follows the layout the backend passes to its own
  matrix-multiply shaders. Apache-2.0, as the repository.

narrow_f32_branch.glsl
  Written for this project: the branch of aii_matmul_f32.comp for a product
  with one output column. Apache-2.0, as the repository.

